<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified"><xs:annotation><xs:documentation>
      Operome: OperomeStGBBodily
      Source: StGB consolidated, offences against bodily integrity (provenance StGB 223, 225, 228; German governs)
      Rebuilt to the current encoding contract, superseding the earlier bodily-integrity carrier. Section 224 has moved
      to Excluded in the working document: the DangerousBodilyHarm scope is withdrawn and in-corpus references to 224
      (the 129a catalogue text) resolve as input only. The 228 scope is new: the consent exception, whole provision
      live, [ConsentJustification] consumed by the Section 13 master rule's {ExceptionActApplies} alongside the 32 and
      34 scopes and limited by the 35 counter-exception; its act element resolves against [BodilyHarm] of the 223 scope
      in this carrier; the good-morals threshold is evaluative residue flagged for escalation.
      Runtime caveat: consolidated file, not a proven executable, until the loader's scope-local resolution is tested.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, Offences Against Bodily Integrity (§223 to §228)</Subject><Verb>protect</Verb><Article>StGB 223, 225, 228</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBBodily</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>

